From: Athos Ribeiro <athos@ubuntu.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Apr 2026 16:51:13 +0800
Subject: Do not default to weak encryption algorithms

Bug-Ubuntu: https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/krb5/+bug/2144909
Last-Update: 2026-03-19

As described in [1], arcfour-hmac-md5 and des3-cbc-sha1 are weak, deprecated
algorithms. However, krb5 still includes them in its default algorithm lists
when users do not specify a list with algorithms to be used. This patch drops
these two deprecated algorithms from that default list.

[1] https://web.mit.edu/kerberos/krb5-1.20/doc/admin/enctypes.html#enctype-compatibility
Last-Update: 2026-03-19
---
 doc/conf.py                 | 2 +-
 src/lib/krb5/krb/init_ctx.c | 2 --
 src/tests/t_authdata.py     | 6 ++++--
 src/tests/t_etype_info.py   | 7 ++++---
 src/tests/t_keyrollover.py  | 2 +-
 src/tests/t_sesskeynego.py  | 9 +++++----
 src/util/k5test.py          | 7 ++++++-
 7 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

